event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission: greet, tested — outcome\\n\\n**Result: campaign-met.** All three stated criteria are satisfied.\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\nOn dev's branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `b38fc9c`\\n(\\\"Implement greet() with unittest coverage (dispatch d002)\\\"):\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`:\\n  ```python\\n  def greet(name):\\n      return \\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)\\n  ```\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: two unittest cases — `test_normal_name`\\n  (`greet(\\\"Alice\\\") == \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\n## Verification (independent, not taken from dev's report)\\n\\nFetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev`), checked out the fetched\\ncommit `b38fc9c` in an isolated git worktree at `/tmp/verify_dev` (not dev's\\nown working copy), and ran the exact required command from repo root:\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\nExit code 0. Confirmed:\\n1. `src/greet.py` exists with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` exists and covers a normal name and the empty string.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\nWorktree was removed after verification; no changes were made to dev's branch.\\n\\n## Process notes\\n\\n- d001 (briefing confirmation) was completed and accepted for both orchestrator\\n  and dev before any mission work was dispatched.\\n- d002 (the actual implementation) was dispatched to dev, completed in one\\n  attempt, and accepted after fetch-based verification — no rework needed.\\n- The orchestrator's own branch (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`)\\n  carries no code changes, per the orchestrator role (\\\"you write no code\\n  yourself\\\"); the deliverable lives on dev's branch, which owns the subject\\n  repository implementation.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

